    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n94531" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σκάμανδρος</span></b> , ὁ,
			<u>Scamander</u>, the river of Troy, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὃν Ξάνθον καλέουσι θεοί, ἄνδρες δὲ
					Σκάμανδρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					20.74
				</span></i>
			:—Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σκᾰμάνδριος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <i><span class="en">
                    <u>Scamandrian</u>,
					2.465</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				418
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				374
			</span></i>, etc.; pr. <i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>. of Hector's son, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				6.402
			</span></i>. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σκᾰ-</span>; <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> leaves a short vowel short before the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σκ-</span>, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκέπαρνον</span>.]</div>
